            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0388" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.00/365.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-28T10:00:00-05:14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1914, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have received from the Minister for Foreign Affairs official information that
                    Dr. Alfredo B. Moreno, President of the Senate arrived in Quito yesterday and
                    has assumed the duties of the Presidency during the absence of President Plaza
                    at Esmeraldas. Matters here have quieted down and the President’s three little
                    sons and nurses have left this Legation and returned to the President’s house.
                    Mrs. Plaza has left the Chilean Legation and is at home.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
